ical, construction, and other industries. It also offers recyclable composite mats to customers worldwide; and access road construction, site planning and preparation, environmental protection, erosion control, and site restoration services. The company was formerly known as Newpark Resources, Inc. and changed its name to NPK International Inc. in December 2024. The company was founded in 1932 and is headquartered in The Woodlands, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Matthew S. Lanigan | President, CEO & Director | Age 54 | Compensation: $4.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 510 people. Revenue per employee of $543K ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers, with revenue falling 8%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $52K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $11K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 8\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["NPK International Inc. is a small-cap industrials business with a $718M market cap on $277M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -30% over the past three years and -9% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 4% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $26M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 9 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.87\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA.","Shareholder yield of 3.2% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 4.7% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 1.5\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Industrials peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Price sits 22% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.2192440356367427},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (86% sell ratio, net $2.6M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 37% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Understanding Momentum Shifts in (NPKI)","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/151/Understanding_Momentum_Shifts_in_NPKI_112726014602_1795805162.html","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795805162.0,"origin":"tiingo","sen